tment plant.<br /> Some slightly less gruesome outcomes could have me get embraced by a vampire recluse for company or someone looking for someone to assist them with managing logistics and records of something. How that relationship plays out is dependant on the sire and how they treat me. I will never willingly join another cult of dogma or personality every again so that rules out the traditional five.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Know what? The boring project you are working on right now in your corp, you know what I mean, that thing you are doing on Monday... it is not what you think it is. Yes really. <br /> You just don\u00b4t know what it is... So you are a VERY important person over night... The vampires want you as their inside man!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13653-narr666","name":"Narr666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T10:15:15-07:00","id":1122384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ameraaaaaa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122280#post1122280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A well what about be being gangril also ether cathen or orde drkul I'd hope to be a bloodline good for combat and be the guy who takes care of punksthat need taking care of then as i become more powerful I'd rule though force and by as much goules and full vampire goons as possible then try and take over other places with vampires until i gain a vampire kingdom full of loyal subjects</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's certainly one way to go about it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T11:23:16-07:00","id":1122405,"title":"","content":"As stated in the other thread, I'd probably end up an unaligned Nosferatu. If I decided to join a Covenant it would most likely be the Carthians, with Lancea et Sanctum as my second choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T14:00:03-07:00","id":1122469,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd much prefer to be a Gangrel, turned at the age of 14-18 when I was at my most athletic, casually exploring abandoned buildings and ravines and the like for fun.<br /> Plus, I've got a reputation for being resilient, various fires and automobile accidents and I've only ever broken my arm - and even then I walked my bike home with a pretty clear head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T15:14:49-07:00","id":1122515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire#post1121995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all, Korogra here again! In order to pass the time on my phone and because these sorts of threads are typically amusing and a fun way to kill time, let us ponder on one of the most obvious questions one could ask: If you were one of the Kindred, what sort of vampire would you be? What is your clan ( and the reason why), which of the covenants did you get sucked into, if any, and what would you would typically be doing in vampiric society? To break the Ice, I'll start us off:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <i>(Put some more thought into it, this time.)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm, I would personally have to say Nosferatu would be my clan, with my embrace being a step up from my current lifestyle. I'm not very educated or attractive to be around, but I have proven to be quite manipulative when I want to, and there have been times when I quickly respond to a situation without having to think about it. It's possible the Nosferatu may be looking to help me cultivate these skills into something useful to (their) society. Plus, I was that kid who was intentionally weird or creepy in school just to get a reaction out of people. So I might just fit right in with the other Nosferatu pranksters. I might even be a Nightmare prodigy and not realize it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am not a political person, so my choice of covenant would be based on other agendas than arguing over which traditions to value. I would be immediately drawn to the Circle of the Crone as soon as I found out they were practicing actual magic (that works). I have always been fascinated by magic and mysticism. When I was younger, I was a true believer in its power and often hoped of coming across a legitimate spell book from time to time. But with my pain tolerance being what it is, I doubt I'd advance very far in Cruac unless I went through some intense physical training.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second option would be remaining Unaligned and trying to stay out of everybody's way unless they picked a fight with me first. Though I'd still be a Circle sympathizer, even if I wasn't a fully recognized member. I wouldn't be a member of the Ordo because I don't have the attention span for it, and I would never join the Lancea because I already renounced Catholicism twice. The Invictus are powerful, but laughably outdated and the Carthians simply don't interest me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for nightly activities, I imagine I'd find work as either a background informant or hired security (putting that clan's Potence to good use). If I were unaligned, my services would be based on pragmatism. Whichever client is most beneficial to me would get my cooperation, regardless of our previous dealings. If I joined the Circle, however, my goals would probably be centered around the pursuit of occult knowledge and magical power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-29-2017, 10:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T00:09:04-07:00","id":1122633,"title":"","content":"Being the sexy emotional wreck that I am I think I'd perfectly fit with the Daeva","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T11:34:06-07:00","id":1122750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122515#post1122515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <i>(Put some more thought into it, this time.)</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Hmmm, I would personally have to say Nosferatu would be my clan, with my embrace being a step up from my current lifestyle. I'm not very educated or attractive to be around, but I have proven to be quite manipulative when I want to, and there have been times when I quickly respond to a situation without having to think about it. It's possible the Nosferatu may be looking to help me cultivate these skills into something useful to (their) society. Plus, I was that kid who was intentionally weird or creepy in school just to get a reaction out of people. So I might just fit right in with the other Nosferatu pranksters. I might even be a Nightmare prodigy and not realize it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am not a political person, so my choice of covenant would be based on other agendas than arguing over which traditions to value. I would be immediately drawn to the Circle of the Crone as soon as I found out they were practicing actual magic (that works). I have always been fascinated by magic and mysticism. When I was younger, I was a true believer in its power and often hoped of coming across a legitimate spell book from time to time. But with my pain tolerance being what it is, I doubt I'd advance very far in Cruac unless I went through some intense physical training.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The second option would be remaining Unaligned and trying to stay out of everybody's way unless they picked a fight with me first. Though I'd still be a Circle sympathizer, even if I wasn't a fully recognized member. I wouldn't be a member of the Ordo because I don't have the attention span for it, and I would never join the Lancea because I already renounced Catholicism twice. The Invictus are powerful, but laughably outdated and the Carthians simply don't interest me.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for nightly activities, I imagine I'd find work as either a background informant or hired security (putting that clan's Potence to good use). If I were unaligned, my services would be based on pragmatism. Whichever client is most beneficial to me would get my cooperation, regardless of our previous dealings. If I joined the Circle, however, my goals would probably be centered around the pursuit of occult knowledge and magical power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that doesn't sound so bad for an eternity. Maybe one day you'd be a mover and shaker","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T11:35:22-07:00","id":1122753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122633#post1122633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being the sexy emotional wreck that I am I think I'd perfectly fit with the Daeva</div> </div> </div> </div>Whys that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T11:39:14-07:00","id":1122754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arduras</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122469#post1122469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I'd much prefer to be a Gangrel, turned at the age of 14-18 when I was at my most athletic, casually exploring abandoned buildings and ravines and the like for fun.<br /> Plus, I've got a reputation for being resilient, various fires and automobile accidents and I've only ever broken my arm - and even then I walked my bike home with a pretty clear head.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few are as resilient as the Gangrel fortunately; Vampire un life is considerably more dangerous than simple fires or car accidents haha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T11:48:07-07:00","id":1122758,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I can see myself as belonging to any clan given the right circumstances, but in general I think I would go with a Mental/Social/Physical Attribute, Social/Mental/Physical Skill Daeva. My sire Embraces me because, despite the fact that I'm generally considered attractive in a bearish way, I don't rely on my looks to get ahead. My sire's the kind of Daeva who believes that the head on your shoulders is usually more useful than the body it rests on. And even in life, people just liked me: I could be friendly and strike up a conversation with pretty much anybody. <br /> <br /> I initially turn to the Ordo because their scholasticism and focus on evolving the vampiric condition attracts me (and let's face it, who <i>doesn't </i>want to join the covenant founded by Count Freaking Dracula?), but old habits die hard and the whole &quot;spit in the face of God and make him allow it&quot; is too blasphemous for my Catholic upbringing to stand. Still, I stay on professional terms and am allowed access to their archives and such from time to time. The Circle of the Crone appeals to my long-standing fascination with mythology, but the violence of their rituals repulses me; still, they know how to party. The Carthians sound pretty cool (vampires who like democracy? Sign me up!) but eventually I see how far they are willing to go to achieve their ideals, and I've had enough experience in life with extreme politics to know how that ends. The Lancea et Sanctum naturally appeals to my Catholic upbringing, but it's just a little too blasphemous for my tastes. Finally, I settle on the Invictus, because they may be monsters, but we're all monsters, and ultimately pragmatism is more valuable to me than ideology. But since I was careful enough to not burn bridges with the others, I find myself in a unique position to act as an emissary for the Invictus to the other covenants. <br /> <br /> I get a reputation as the &quot;reasonable&quot; or &quot;cool&quot; Invictus neonate, not one of those stuck-up, stuffy ones. It's amazing how far a little respect and civility can go in the All-Night Society. I have allies and contacts in every covenant, and I'm constantly presenting the perspectives of the Invictus to the other covenants, and vice versa- calmly, politely, frankly. I never resort to violence, I leave that to the knights, I just turn my head and mutter something about rabid dogs needing to be put down. Within the Invictus, I don't present myself as ambitious (because that's a death sentence), but I'm always on the lookout when people further up the food chain drop the ball, and I'm always there picking up the slack, doing whatever my superiors need me to. Eventually, I'm just too useful and loyal to let die. I'm everybody's friend, no way are the elders going to let some neonate or ancilla off me. And after decades of networking and hard work, I win the eye of the Prince and become Seneschal, the most trusted vampire in the domain. And then, after a century or two, the Prince announces their impending torpor, and the crown passes to the only man he can trust to keep the ship on course: me, the nice Daeva who, through a long process of favors and a nice friendly attitude, has the backing and support of every elder in the domain. And maybe, when the Prince reawakens, the elders don't want him to take the reins back. Because who do they trust more, the guy who's been out of commission for a century or so, or the guy who's been working his butt off with a smile on his face to keep things going smoothly?<br /> <br /> ... Dear Lord, I've given this way too much thought.<br /> <br /> TL;DR A Daeva who avoids the whole &quot;vampire sex god&quot; shtick to focus on becoming a spokesman and emissary for the Invictus, and works his way up the ladder through a combination of good personality, competence, strong work ethic, and a healthy sense of realpolitik.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:07:24-07:00","id":1122766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122750#post1122750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, that doesn't sound so bad for an eternity. Maybe one day you'd be a mover and shaker</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">And deal with the headache of managing a bunch of 300 year old politicians?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">No thank you!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sitting close to the throne can be more comfortable than sitting atop it.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-30-2017, 03:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:07:41-07:00","id":1122767,"title":"","content":"I usually think that, realistically speaking, if I lived in the CoD setting I'd probably be dead, broken or a thrall to supernaturals. Possibly all of that, to be honest.<br /> <br /> That said, if I happened to become a Vampire, I'll probably join the Ordo Dracul. It's all about the Coils. Since I gotta deal with unlife, I might as well try to limit the negative sides where I can. I don't need exclusive powers or a place of importance in a court of corpses, but if you tell me there's a way I can make everday existence easier on a practical side, I'm sold. Vampires rank a bit low on my personal &quot;list of CoD splats I'd like to be&quot;, so you can understand.<br /> <br /> As for Clan...I have no idea. Anybody has suggestions?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:12:00-07:00","id":1122768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122758#post1122758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I can see myself as belonging to any clan given the right circumstances, but in general I think I would go with a Mental/Social/Physical Attribute, Social/Mental/Physical Skill Daeva. My sire Embraces me because, despite the fact that I'm generally considered attractive in a bearish way, I don't rely on my looks to get ahead. My sire's the kind of Daeva who believes that the head on your shoulders is usually more useful than the body it rests on. And even in life, people just liked me: I could be friendly and strike up a conversation with pretty much anybody. <br /> <br /> I initially turn to the Ordo because their scholasticism and focus on evolving the vampiric condition attracts me (and let's face it, who <i>doesn't </i>want to join the covenant founded by Count Freaking Dracula?), but old habits die hard and the whole &amp;quot;spit in the face of God and make him allow it&amp;quot; is too blasphemous for my Catholic upbringing to stand. Still, I stay on professional terms and am allowed access to their archives and such from time to time. The Circle of the Crone appeals to my long-standing fascination with mythology, but the violence of their rituals repulses me; still, they know how to party. The Carthians sound pretty cool (vampires who like democracy? Sign me up!) but eventually I see how far they are willing to go to achieve their ideals, and I've had enough experience in life with extreme politics to know how that ends. The Lancea et Sanctum naturally appeals to my Catholic upbringing, but it's just a little too blasphemous for my tastes. Finally, I settle on the Invictus, because they may be monsters, but we're all monsters, and ultimately pragmatism is more valuable to me than ideology. But since I was careful enough to not burn bridges with the others, I find myself in a unique position to act as an emissary for the Invictus to the other covenants. <br /> <br /> I get a reputation as the &amp;quot;reasonable&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;cool&amp;quot; Invictus neonate, not one of those stuck-up, stuffy ones. It's amazing how far a little respect and civility can go in the All-Night Society. I have allies and contacts in every covenant, and I'm constantly presenting the perspectives of the Invictus to the other covenants, and vice versa- calmly, politely, frankly. I never resort to violence, I leave that to the knights, I just turn my head and mutter something about rabid dogs needing to be put down. Within the Invictus, I don't present myself as ambitious (because that's a death sentence), but I'm always on the lookout when people further up the food chain drop the ball, and I'm always there picking up the slack, doing whatever my superiors need me to. Eventually, I'm just too useful and loyal to let die. I'm everybody's friend, no way are the elders going to let some neonate or ancilla off me. And after decades of networking and hard work, I win the eye of the Prince and become Seneschal, the most trusted vampire in the domain. And then, after a century or two, the Prince announces their impending torpor, and the crown passes to the only man he can trust to keep the ship on course: me, the nice Daeva who, through a long process of favors and a nice friendly attitude, has the backing and support of every elder in the domain. And maybe, when the Prince reawakens, the elders don't want him to take the reins back. Because who do they trust more, the guy who's been out of commission for a century or so, or the guy who's been working his butt off with a smile on his face to keep things going smoothly?<br /> <br /> ... Dear Lord, I've given this way too much thought.<br /> <br /> TL;DR A Daeva who avoids the whole &amp;quot;vampire sex god&amp;quot; shtick to focus on becoming a spokesman and emissary for the Invictus, and works his way up the ladder through a combination of good personality, competence, strong work ethic, and a healthy sense of realpolitik.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this because it's not to dissimilar from how I'd go about it. Now while I'm not Catholic, my Baptist upbringing makes all the religious Covenants too unappealing, though I would say that maybe a couple of centuries down the road the Lancea Et Sanctum might strike an accord once my vampire existence finally fully bleeds into my world views","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:17:55-07:00","id":1122769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122767#post1122767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Clan...I have no idea. Anybody has suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Without knowing more about you on a personal level, I don't think anybody can recommend a clan. It all comes down to whether or not you have something that the clan is looking to add to their ranks. As I said, I have a knack for subterfuge and going with my instincts over formal training, which is why I think the Nosferatu would be interested in me. So what talents do you think would make you a useful candidate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T12:27:28-07:00","id":1122773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122767#post1122767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I usually think that, realistically speaking, if I lived in the CoD setting I'd probably be dead, broken or a thrall to supernaturals. Possibly all of that, to be honest.<br /> <br /> That said, if I happened to become a Vampire, I'll probably join the Ordo Dracul. It's all about the Coils. Since I gotta deal with unlife, I might as well try to limit the negative sides where I can. I don't need exclusive powers or a place of importance in a court of corpses, but if you tell me there's a way I can make everday existence easier on a practical side, I'm sold. Vampires rank a bit low on my personal &amp;quot;list of CoD splats I'd like to be&amp;quot;, so you can understand.<br /> <br /> As for Clan...I have no idea. Anybody has suggestions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mekhet or Gangrel maybe? Nosferatu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:14:38-07:00","id":1122788,"title":"","content":"I haven't put a lot of thought into this, but:<br /> <br /> I am good at research, at digging up information, at contextualizing it, and at connecting the dots to produce educated guesses about information I do not have. I think I'd be Mekhet because of that. I have a tendency to create personas for different social contexts that would probably serve me well with some aspects of Obfuscate and doing Mekhet stuff.<br /> <br /> As far as covenant goes, I'd either end up in the Circle of the Crone because of my religious leanings or the Carthians because of my political leanings (or possibly a bit of both with either the Chorister or Casual User merits). If in the Circle of the Crone I'm not sure I'd go all in on the sheer bloodiness of the covenant, at least not at first. It'd take a bit of time to work through my &quot;humanity&quot; to the point that it becomes, if not <i>acceptable,</i> then <i>tolerable</i>. That might take some time, however. If Carthian, I'm not sure where precisely I'd end up. I know that Carthians also use their political leanings and connections as a means to an end that humans do not, because <i>vampire</i> but my thoughts on this are not fully formed at this time. I do know that when I've been in organizations and movements in real life that I tend to make a good impression and sometimes make my way up the ladder a bit relatively easily. That may be the case in the Carthians moreso than in the Circle. Aaaand thinking about it now I think I'd probably go Carthian with Chorister merit.<br /> <br /> I don't really have any long-term stuff in mind. It seems to me that surviving and thriving as a neonate is a pretty monumental task on its own, and I'm not really up to planning that far ahead yet. If I were to play myself as this character then certainly plans would develop over time as I become a part of the Carthian and city's social fabric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T13:42:23-07:00","id":1122795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122768#post1122768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like this because it's not to dissimilar from how I'd go about it. Now while I'm not Catholic, my Baptist upbringing makes all the religious Covenants too unappealing, though I would say that maybe a couple of centuries down the road the Lancea Et Sanctum might strike an accord once my vampire existence finally fully bleeds into my world views</div> </div> </div> </div>I would eventually come to see the Sanctified as a decent way of keeping a lid on the local humans- &quot;Archbishop, the First Estate can no longer tolerate the existence of the Broad Street Slasher. If you could send your best men to find and eliminate this menace, we would be indebted.&quot; <br /> <br /> I think I would be Sanctified if I got Embraced as a Nosferatu. Literally seeing myself twisted into a monster, I think the Sanctified would make a lot of head way if they came to me with a pitch like, &quot;You are damned, but you can still serve God if you help us hunt down the wicked and punish them.&quot;<br /> <br /> In general, Requiem works very well on an archetypal level that everybody is going to be able to see a little bit of each clan in themselves. And that's the fun of it, I think: identifying one of your character flaws (or who knows, maybe even one your good traits) and translating it into a clan/covenant combination.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:35:50-07:00","id":1122838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122788#post1122788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't put a lot of thought into this, but:<br /> <br /> I am good at research, at digging up information, at contextualizing it, and at connecting the dots to produce educated guesses about information I do not have. I think I'd be Mekhet because of that. I have a tendency to create personas for different social contexts that would probably serve me well with some aspects of Obfuscate and doing Mekhet stuff.<br /> <br /> As far as covenant goes, I'd either end up in the Circle of the Crone because of my religious leanings or the Carthians because of my political leanings (or possibly a bit of both with either the Chorister or Casual User merits). If in the Circle of the Crone I'm not sure I'd go all in on the sheer bloodiness of the covenant, at least not at first. It'd take a bit of time to work through my &quot;humanity&quot; to the point that it becomes, if not <i>acceptable,</i> then <i>tolerable</i>. That might take some time, however. If Carthian, I'm not sure where precisely I'd end up. I know that Carthians also use their political leanings and connections as a means to an end that humans do not, because <i>vampire</i> but my thoughts on this are not fully formed at this time. I do know that when I've been in organizations and movements in real life that I tend to make a good impression and sometimes make my way up the ladder a bit relatively easily. That may be the case in the Carthians moreso than in the Circle. Aaaand thinking about it now I think I'd probably go Carthian with Chorister merit.<br /> <br /> I don't really have any long-term stuff in mind. It seems to me that surviving and thriving as a neonate is a pretty monumental task on its own, and I'm not really up to planning that far ahead yet. If I were to play myself as this character then certainly plans would develop over time as I become a part of the Carthian and city's social fabric.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I fully get behind playing a Mekhet like that, I just can't ever see the appeal of the Crone. Like the Lance, it's playing on becoming a divinely ordained Predator, and while I buy into the adaptation and evolution bit ( that's part of why I love Gangrel so much, they are ever changing)... it's too close to the Beast and therefore the Strix for my liking lol<br /> <br /> Now you never have to play it that way, in fact one of my favorite stories in the Strix Chronicles Anthology is Owl Sign and it has one of the most relatable Acolytes I've ever seen... but still lol","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:40:50-07:00","id":1122841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122795#post1122795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would eventually come to see the Sanctified as a decent way of keeping a lid on the local humans- &amp;quot;Archbishop, the First Estate can no longer tolerate the existence of the Broad Street Slasher. If you could send your best men to find and eliminate this menace, we would be indebted.&amp;quot; <br /> <br /> I think I would be Sanctified if I got Embraced as a Nosferatu. Literally seeing myself twisted into a monster, I think the Sanctified would make a lot of head way if they came to me with a pitch like, &amp;quot;You are damned, but you can still serve God if you help us hunt down the wicked and punish them.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> In general, Requiem works very well on an archetypal level that everybody is going to be able to see a little bit of each clan in themselves. And that's the fun of it, I think: identifying one of your character flaws (or who knows, maybe even one your good traits) and translating it into a clan/covenant combination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed, I think I'd come around to a similar point of view eventual were I one of the Kindred, though I'd still try to keep most of my mortal beliefs in order to help my hold on Hunanity be that much stronger. True faith does not need the physical temple after all .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T16:45:09-07:00","id":1122844,"title":"","content":"As far as Clan goes, I'd most likely wind up either a Mekhet who dabbles in Animalism early on, or (less likely) an Animalism-focused Ventrue with a similar amount of dabbling in Obfuscate and just enough Dominate to pry secrets out of people or make them just, y'know... &quot;fuck off for awhile&quot;. And I'd probably get it into my head to seek out or eventually try to create a Bloodline that yielded in-clan Dominate and/or Animalism (if Mekhet) with Celerity being dropped if opting for both, or Auspex (if Ventrue) and maybe Obfuscate in exchange for Resilience.<br /> <br /> For Covenant, knowing me I'd either be unaligned or splitting my allegiance three ways between the Carthians, the Circle of the Crone, and the Ordo Dracul. The Carthians as less of a front-liner and more of the &quot;set you up with info and a place to stay&quot; type, since my political leanings aren't going to just disappear through the Embrace but I'm, ah, not the most physically capable on a mundane level; the Circle as a way to explore the spiritual aspects and see if they clicked where mortal stuff hasn't, and to get a basic feel for <i>actual literal magic</i>; the Ordo... the Ordo would be out of a combination of sheer self-serving curiosity about Everything That Goes Bump and a desire to patch up whatever issues carried over from my living body, with some study of the actual Coils carrying over from there.<br /> <br /> Eventually, particularly once the ol' Humanity dropped a bit and settled, I'd probably be the sort to start funneling bits of non-vampire-y supernatural info (and some low-end maybe-cursed-maybe-just-magical trinkets) to some of the small-town paranormal investigator types. A haunting here, a weird animal sighting there... if they live and report back, that's some additional info in my pocket and perhaps some new allies (maybe even eventual ghouls, if they keep coming back), and if they die then that's fewer potential hunters to cause trouble down the line and a distinct &quot;Do Not Go Here Unprepared&quot; warning to spread among associates and existing allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 07-30-2017, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T20:53:23-07:00","id":1122892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122838#post1122838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I fully get behind playing a Mekhet like that, I just can't ever see the appeal of the Crone. Like the Lance, it's playing on becoming a divinely ordained Predator, and while I buy into the adaptation and evolution bit ( that's part of why I love Gangrel so much, they are ever changing)... it's too close to the Beast and therefore the Strix for my liking lol<br /> <br /> Now you never have to play it that way, in fact one of my favorite stories in the Strix Chronicles Anthology is Owl Sign and it has one of the most relatable Acolytes I've ever seen... but still lol</div> </div> </div> </div>It's fine if you don't see the appeal of the Crone, because you didn't make my post. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I do see the appeal of the Crone, although I admit that they are pretty savage and bloodthirsty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:36:51-07:00","id":1122901,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu, Carthian or Circle. I'll dig up the explanation from last time this convo happened and then add one why possibly Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T21:52:38-07:00","id":1122907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122753#post1122753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whys that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm an emotionally volatile, easily agitated teenager who is considered physically attractive by many people, if that's not Daeva I don't know what is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T23:48:15-07:00","id":1122927,"title":"","content":"If I got to make all the choices, let's see. I would be a Mekhet since I generally prefer to blend into the background and observe others already. Upon learning of the existence of spirits, ghosts, and strix, I would try to become a Khaibit to provide as much protection as I could from such things.<br /> <br /> I would find the religious covenants a bit frightening. The hypocrisy of the Carthians would annoy me enough that I would probably try to bring them down if I could get away with it cleanly. I might affiliate with the Invictus but the power struggle thing wouldn't interest me, so I wouldn't want to join. The goal of transcendence the Ordo Dracul has is similar to evolution so I would give that a try. I think I would go for the Mystery of the Ascendant. I'm not sure if I would be interested or successful in Dragon politics, and I know I would avoid joining the Sworn of the Axe. If I felt the need to become involved in vampire society generally then I would try working with the sheriff.<br /> <br /> I would try to find a Gangrel to make friends with so I could learn out of clan disciplines. Of the remaining three clans, the mental disciplines wouldn't interest me much. I think the most useful would be Majesty, but I don't like to be the center of attention, so I don't know that would work out. I suppose given enough time I might become jaded enough to think Dominate was a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:20:59-07:00","id":1123061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122927#post1122927\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I got to make all the choices, let's see. I would be a Mekhet since I generally prefer to blend into the background and observe others already. Upon learning of the existence of spirits, ghosts, and strix, I would try to become a Khaibit to provide as much protection as I could from such things.<br /> <br /> I would find the religious covenants a bit frightening. The hypocrisy of the Carthians would annoy me enough that I would probably try to bring them down if I could get away with it cleanly. I might affiliate with the Invictus but the power struggle thing wouldn't interest me, so I wouldn't want to join. The goal of transcendence the Ordo Dracul has is similar to evolution so I would give that a try. I think I would go for the Mystery of the Ascendant. I'm not sure if I would be interested or successful in Dragon politics, and I know I would avoid joining the Sworn of the Axe. If I felt the need to become involved in vampire society generally then I would try working with the sheriff.<br /> <br /> I would try to find a Gangrel to make friends with so I could learn out of clan disciplines. Of the remaining three clans, the mental disciplines wouldn't interest me much. I think the most useful would be Majesty, but I don't like to be the center of attention, so I don't know that would work out. I suppose given enough time I might become jaded enough to think Dominate was a good idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it bad that out of all of the ( two) actually stated out 2nd ed bloodlines Khaibit are the coolest shit ever?<br /> <br /> hm, Sworn of the Dying Light is a pretty good Sworn to be part of if you're more of the Scholarly bent.<br /> <br /> Well, if you are looking for a badass friend, you never can go wrong with a Gangrel XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-31-2017, 01:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:29:33-07:00","id":1123064,"title":"","content":"So I forgot that you can be a member of two covenants without having to take those 2 pt merits so I'm slightly changing my answer to &quot;I'd have Carthian and Crone membership.&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree that the Khaibit are indeed the coolest shit ever. Made me get the books they appeared in to get more information. Not sure I'd personally want to be one, but not sure I wouldn't want to be. I may revisit the bloodline question later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T10:38:36-07:00","id":1123067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1123064#post1123064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I forgot that you can be a member of two covenants without having to take those 2 pt merits so I'm slightly changing my answer to &quot;I'd have Carthian and Crone membership.&quot;<br /> <br /> I agree that the Khaibit are indeed the coolest shit ever. Made me get the books they appeared in to get more information. Not sure I'd personally want to be one, but not sure I wouldn't want to be. I may revisit the bloodline question later.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of Bloodlines, since I completely forgot about those... I'd probably be a Shepard, considering my protective instincts XD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 07-31-2017, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:04:14-07:00","id":1123098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1123061#post1123061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it bad that out of all of the ( two) actually stated out 2nd ed bloodlines Khaibit are the coolest shit ever?<br /> <br /> hm, Sworn of the Dying Light is a pretty good Sworn to be part of if you're more of the Scholarly bent.<br /> <br /> Well, if you are looking for a badass friend, you never can go wrong with a Gangrel XD</div> </div> </div> </div>No, although I would be more drawn to the ephemeral combat and darkness sight more than anything. Otherwise, I wouldn't bother with a Mekhet bloodline. Scholar or diplomat would be a tough decision. Either fits me better than warrior. I'm not sure I would be interested in a Dragon's idea of &quot;research&quot;. I would probably only join for the coils which apparently is pretty common. A badass friend wouldn't hurt, but I would focus on Protean teacher. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Gangrel would actually be my second choice but the Mekhet role probably fits me better, a bit half-Mekhet and half-Gangrel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T12:35:46-07:00","id":1123117,"title":"","content":"I don't see how I would appeal to any clan, but I'm superficially a bit closer to Mekhet, so I'll go with that.<br /> <br /> If we were talking about covenants working in mortal interests, I'd pick the Carthians, no runner up. I don't know if I would extend the same standards to vampires though. If I last more than a few months though, I expect that I'd start to justify my own continued existence in which I'd be inclined to do the same for other vampires and that's when I'd decide that we need government.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum could be tempting if they lead with the history, relics and occult stuff with some miracles to demonstrate their significance, especially if they're something like the Westminister Creed; even when I was religious, I became disillusioned with the ritualistic trappings that I commonly perceived within my own sect. I might feed using the internet a lot of the time in which case there would probably be a psychotic Spear somewhere thinking &quot;Splendid! We can groom him on the sly into a Craigslist mass murderer to pick off degenerates like him as an example so that the mortals keep it in their pants outside marriage!&quot;. But then where I live, they're probably propping up Invictus more than doing their own job.<br /> <br /> I'd like to chat to acolytes and try to learn about their ways and ideas, but I wouldn't accept an invitation to join their ceremonies or spy on them unless I was pushed by own covenant. But then, if my own covenant wanted me out, they could say &quot;You're friendly with the Crones. Get closer to them and tell us what they're up to,&quot;. Then the Circle would pretend they believed that I was interested in joining them and sacrifice me*. Maybe if I just make my reasons for not being trustworthy to the Circle open and clear from the start, that wouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> It would take a good sales pitch get me into join the Ordo Dracul, which isn't their style. If I was embraced into it, I think I'd be less inclined to leave it than most covenants though.<br /> <br /> I'd only be in Invictus for convenience, but they're good at making themselves the convenient option (as a member or a tolerated outsider pleb).<br /> <br /> *<br /> Carthian: Oh noes. The Circle of Crone murdered Spencer. Those fiends.<br /> Acolyte: Libel. We only sacrifice Mekhet on new moons.<br /> Sheriff: Look, do you want to press charges or not? I've got a game of blood golf with the boys tonight.<br /> Carthian: Um, no, we don't, because of... realpolitik.<br /> Sheriff: You're all about realpolitik, aren't you?<br /> Carthian: Haha, yes. Our means may be questionable now, but it will be worth it when the people overthrow your despotic, dated regime!<br /> Sheriff: Mhmm, that's nice. I think I can hear my helicopter landing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","user":"Spencer from The Hills","date":". 07-31-2017, 03:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T12:27:38-07:00","id":1123595,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1123117#post1123117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how I would appeal to any clan, but I'm superficially a bit closer to Mekhet, so I'll go with that.<br /> <br /> If we were talking about covenants working in mortal interests, I'd pick the Carthians, no runner up. I don't know if I would extend the same standards to vampires though. If I last more than a few months though, I expect that I'd start to justify my own continued existence in which I'd be inclined to do the same for other vampires and that's when I'd decide that we need government.<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum could be tempting if they lead with the history, relics and occult stuff with some miracles to demonstrate their significance, especially if they're something like the Westminister Creed; even when I was religious, I became disillusioned with the ritualistic trappings that I commonly perceived within my own sect. I might feed using the internet a lot of the time in which case there would probably be a psychotic Spear somewhere thinking &amp;quot;Splendid! We can groom him on the sly into a Craigslist mass murderer to pick off degenerates like him as an example so that the mortals keep it in their pants outside marriage!&amp;quot;. But then where I live, they're probably propping up Invictus more than doing their own job.<br /> <br /> I'd like to chat to acolytes and try to learn about their ways and ideas, but I wouldn't accept an invitation to join their ceremonies or spy on them unless I was pushed by own covenant. But then, if my own covenant wanted me out, they could say &amp;quot;You're friendly with the Crones. Get closer to them and tell us what they're up to,&amp;quot;. Then the Circle would pretend they believed that I was interested in joining them and sacrifice me*. Maybe if I just make my reasons for not being trustworthy to the Circle open and clear from the start, that wouldn't happen.<br /> <br /> It would take a good sales pitch get me into join the Ordo Dracul, which isn't their style. If I was embraced into it, I think I'd be less inclined to leave it than most covenants though.<br /> <br /> I'd only be in Invictus for convenience, but they're good at making themselves the convenient option (as a member or a tolerated outsider pleb).<br /> <br /> *<br /> Carthian: Oh noes. The Circle of Crone murdered Spencer. Those fiends.<br /> Acolyte: Libel. We only sacrifice Mekhet on new moons.<br /> Sheriff: Look, do you want to press charges or not? I've got a game of blood golf with the boys tonight.<br /> Carthian: Um, no, we don't, because of... realpolitik.<br /> Sheriff: You're all about realpolitik, aren't you?<br /> Carthian: Haha, yes. Our means may be questionable now, but it will be worth it when the people overthrow your despotic, dated regime!<br /> Sheriff: Mhmm, that's nice. I think I can hear my helicopter landing</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah yes, Realpolitik at its finest. If you were wanting to be useful but not noticed you could easily be one of the Norvegi. Actually a Carthian Norvegus would be hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T16:12:20-07:00","id":1123683,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: Mekhet or possibly Ventrue<br /> <b>Reason</b>: I tend to be the quiet kind of person, usually. I like to watch others, observe them, analyse things. I love learning stuff. That whole part of Mekhet just feels right to me. On the other hand, I'm the kind of person that people listen to, for whatever reason. I'm not the most charismatic person in the sense that I have a forceful personality, but I guess I'm mostly just very reasonable, and I'm very pragmatic. I don't really want to be a leader of any kind, but I'm the type of person who'll grab it fast as hell if I don't think there's anyone qualified for it, because I can't stand leaders who're doing a bad job of it (assuming it's a leadership position that I'd be qualified for). I also love to debate and argue, and have recently discovered that I like talking in front of people (going to a Toastmaster's club and everything). I think those are qualities that might make a Ventrue take interest. <br /> <br /> <b>Covenenat: </b>Ordo Dracul of the Carthian Movement<br /> <b>Reason</b>: I love politics, new ideas, I'm very progressive. The Carthian Movement feels like a good fit. I also like science, and the idea of studying what it means to be a Vampire and to transcend undeath is also extremely fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11756-razikale","name":"Razikale","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T19:35:55-07:00","id":1123748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122381#post1122381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well... assuming the gruesome did or didn't happen, what do you think you would be?</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I have no idea. If we\u2019re saying selection is based on the notion that vampires only embrace to perpetuate their respective clich\u00e9s, turning people who already exhibit traits that make them desirable to that clan already, the only clan I find unlikely to where it would be obviously contrived if it happened is the Daeva because I have a talent for tuning out supercilious people, I have no interest in socializing in large groups, I don\u2019t care about being popular or follow celebrities. I don\u2019t drink, smoke, use drugs beyond treating the rare illness, visit strip clubs, bars and other \u201cdens of iniquity\u201d so I\u2019d be unlikely to attract one\u2019s attention. If I were to be \u201cchosen\u201d by my profession and favored hobbies, I would say Mekhet or Gangrel because my interests run the gamut; trivia, science, history, occult/religion, photography, animals, archery, camping, and martial arts. If we\u2019re going by personality traits and behavior, I would have to say Nosferatu or Ventrue because I intimidate people without trying (from the high school bully to my brother-in-law who teaches advanced combative courses in the Army) or I come straight to the point about what I want or what I want to accomplish and prefer to ignore the bullshit social niceties and time wasting tasks whenever possible.<br /> If I were given something resembling a choice, I\u2019d want to be Akhud and would be happy to go around destroying other vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Narr666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1122383#post1122383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The boring project you are working on right now in your corp, you know what I mean, that thing you are doing on Monday... it is not what you think it is. Yes really. You just don\u00b4t know what it is... So you are a VERY important person over night... The vampires want you as their inside man!</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the background for one of my other characters that got turned into a vampire. She stumbled across an experiment they were doing that involved using vitae and meteorite dust as GMO components. They were more interested in seeing what she did once she discovered the anomaly and who or if she\u2019d tell. I can assure you though, nothing I do for my current employer is that interesting or useful. But that total solar eclipse is coming up soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 08-01-2017, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T07:17:45-07:00","id":1123867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1123748#post1123748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I have no idea. If we\u2019re saying selection is based on the notion that vampires only embrace to perpetuate their respective clich\u00e9s, turning people who already exhibit traits that make them desirable to that clan already, the only clan I find unlikely to where it would be obviously contrived if it happened is the Daeva because I have a talent for tuning out supercilious people, I have no interest in socializing in large groups, I don\u2019t care about being popular or follow celebrities. I don\u2019t drink, smoke, use drugs beyond treating the rare illness, visit strip clubs, bars and other \u201cdens of iniquity\u201d so I\u2019d be unlikely to attract one\u2019s attention. If I were to be \u201cchosen\u201d by my profession and favored hobbies, I would say Mekhet or Gangrel because my interests run the gamut; trivia, science, history, occult/religion, photography, animals, archery, camping, and martial arts. If we\u2019re going by personality traits and behavior, I would have to say Nosferatu or Ventrue because I intimidate people without trying (from the high school bully to my brother-in-law who teaches advanced combative courses in the Army) or I come straight to the point about what I want or what I want to accomplish and prefer to ignore the bullshit social niceties and time wasting tasks whenever possible.<br /> If I were given something resembling a choice, I\u2019d want to be Akhud and would be happy to go around destroying other vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That was the background for one of my other characters that got turned into a vampire. She stumbled across an experiment they were doing that involved using vitae and meteorite dust as GMO components. They were more interested in seeing what she did once she discovered the anomaly and who or if she\u2019d tell. I can assure you though, nothing I do for my current employer is that interesting or useful. But that total solar eclipse is coming up soon. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#FFFFFF\">Save</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div>Well that is depressing somewhat, but utterly understandable.<br /> <br /> Now to tell the truth, I sympathize greatly with the Akhud, both 1st and 2nd edition versions. I love Gangrel to undeath, and they are always my first choice for these sort of things... Buut if I was embraced into the Akhud, I wouldn't be as conflicted about it as I probably should. The darkest parts of my personality synergizes very well with the outlook of Clan Akhud, far more than I like to admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T10:49:35-07:00","id":1123928,"title":"","content":"Knowing my luck, I'd probably be a Revenant. So here we go.<br /> <br /> Clan: Revenant<br /> <br /> Reason: Based on my luck that's the most likely thing that would happen to me, but if offered the to be inducted to be a full kindred I'd probably be too terrified it whatever the catch is, or to scared to show my face anywhere near other Kindred <br /> <br /> Covenant: More than likely one of the Unaligned, but I could fit into any of the covenants depending on how my unlife went. I'd probably be happiest as one of the Unaligned though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T13:33:11-07:00","id":1123994,"title":"","content":"Clan: Probably Ventrue (if I could choose) or Gangrel (if not)<br /> <br /> Covenant: If I were Ventrue, most likely Invictus. Going to rise to a comfortable position and acquire a modicum of power that makes me more useful than dangerous.<br /> Gangrel, definitly Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> Reason: I would enjoy carving out a place for myself in a given political landscape, if I had a few more tools at hand, I think. Dominate and Animalism might be just that.<br /> I am pretty adaptable, both socially and physically.<br /> Gangrel would fit with my more stubborn streaks, and since I like traveling, I could see myself as a Kindred on the move from city to city. Ordo Dracul because of my own scientific and mythological interests (occult sounds wrong; I like reading about all kinds of stuff like that, but only as a form of cultural fantasy research, I suppose) and a desire to leave my weaknesses behind me.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, Ventrue Ordo Dracul with Coils of the Voivode.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-02T15:43:21-07:00","id":1124046,"title":"","content":"Well this may be cheating but if I could choose, I'd be a ghoul! Again with the choice assumption, I would go with a good friend and/or Daeva as Regnant so they would have a sympathetic connection to me as well and be less inclined to stomp me down before I'd have a chance to adjust and learn enough to discern the truth from lies.<br /> <br /> It seems like a much brighter life to have access to many of the powers and longevity without all that hunger and alienation stuff. I think I would first focus on stacking up Resilience and a little Celerity to hopefully not be swatted like a fly when my Regnant or his Kindred suddenly fly into a murderous rage. They say sugar is as addictive as cocaine and I rarely indulge in that so I think I could cope with the whole addiction thing just fine.<br /> <br /> I've always been fascinated with the natural world so a Gangrel Regnant and knowledge of Protean would be a favorable arrangement as well, assuming again that he/she/it's not inclined to stomp me down.<br /> <br /> If I didn't get to choose, I'd probably end up as a Revenant like <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional\">Ever Professional</a></b> but I would be more interested in quickly gaining enough favor to be uplifed or Diablerizing some Lick because of the living hell that I imagine Revenant..ism?hood? to be. That is of course, if I knew or thought that such a thing would help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","user":"Rathamus","date":". 08-02-2017, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T00:30:20-07:00","id":1124645,"title":"","content":"Well ancient ghouls are just as potent as vampires of similar age, so I don't see it as cheating too badly, though personally I wouldn't want to be a Ghoul- too much of a threat of running out of vitae and rapidly aging to death in my opinion. Sure I'd still be human and have the ability to walk around during the day without getting a really bad tan... but how my life is currently not ever seeing the sun isn't too much of a deterrent of achieving more permanent immortality despite the thirst or the other weaknesses. When you pray for rain you gotta deal with the mud after all XD<br /> <br /> Now those people saying they'd likely start off as Revenants.. that's an interesting if slightly agonizing one. Vampires might suffer from blood thirst, but they at least can sate it for awhile; they aren't starving on a nightly basis. Still, it does offer interesting directions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T09:55:45-07:00","id":1124816,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that as a ghoul, you are infinitely more expendable than a proper vampire.<br /> <br /> Blood bonds and disciplines being what they are, anybody can be turned into an effective, submissive little ghoul.<br /> <br /> A childe you can be proud of, however, is hard to come by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T10:30:07-07:00","id":1124826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1124816#post1124816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that as a ghoul, you are infinitely more expendable than a proper vampire.<br /> <br /> Blood bonds and disciplines being what they are, anybody can be turned into an effective, submissive little ghoul.<br /> <br /> A childe you can be proud of, however, is hard to come by.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is another reason to not want to be a blood slave haha","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:19:19-07:00","id":1124939,"title":"","content":"Not entirely sure what bloodlines (if any), I might belong to. I can't imagine too many Nosferatu bloodlines might be operable where I live, but I'd have to say a likely candidate would be Noctuku.<br /> <br /> Having a craving for vampire flesh isn't that big of an issue when you realize they can regenerate. Sure, it might be painful as hell, but you would make a full recovery by the end of the week. And as a member of either the Circle or the Unaligned, I imagine I'd have no shortage enemies to keep staked in the basement as a self replenishing food source. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:22:10-07:00","id":1124941,"title":"","content":"They would need blood to regenerate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T14:50:22-07:00","id":1124957,"title":"","content":"Not to mention Noctuku are sort of terrifying to be around because of that need to eat flesh. Nosferatu might be uncomfortable to be around, but most of them aren't thinking about gnawing your arm off, even if you can eventually grow a new one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T16:14:33-07:00","id":1124994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1124957#post1124957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention Noctuku are sort of terrifying to be around because of that need to eat flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was my impression that most Noctuku do not announce themselves, unless they're serving as a deterrent for the reigning monarch.<br /> <br /> Also, I think getting them enough blood to recover from the process would be pretty simple. It's not like you're trying to keep them at full power, they just need enough to survive so you don't commit murder every single night.<br /> <br /> <b>Easy solution</b> = Keep a couple Ghouls on hand to force feed the incapacitated prisoners vitae, then when they're in decent enough shape, strip off a couple pounds of flesh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-04-2017, 07:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-04T16:48:12-07:00","id":1125001,"title":"","content":"If we're also picking bloodlines, I'd go with Spina. Because hey, what good is a highly refined sense of deadpan and snark if you can't literally weaponize it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T01:40:42-07:00","id":1125137,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd like to say I'd be clan Daeva...strong, fast, and <i>fascinating</i>.<br /> <br /> But if I'm being totally honest, I'd probably end up being in the Mekhet--I've always been good at gathering information and picking up on things that others don't. I've also always been beneath most people's notice; so much so that my former High School classmates swear I vanished from sight one time; so stealth comes naturally. Plus, the various ticks of my natural personality would probably help adjustment to the various banes Clan Mekhet suffers much easier.<br /> <br /> As for Covenant, the Lancea et Sanctum all the way. Spirituality aside, the philosophy of it just makes sense to me...If I'm destined for corruption in unlife, best to hone it into a weapon with which to strike at the corruption I see in the world. Also, the access to various relics and histories, as well as the magic of Theban Sorcery would probably thrill my cold, dead, unbeating heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1868-hellovg","name":"hellovg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T04:11:50-07:00","id":1125167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125001#post1125001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're also picking bloodlines, I'd go with Spina. Because hey, what good is a highly refined sense of deadpan and snark if you can't literally weaponize it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah the Spina, one of my favorite Bloodlines to use for antagonist roles haha. I love using the final level of their Discipline to give semi fatal Reason You Suck speeches on occasion in my games lol<br /> <br /> Nice choice!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T05:53:10-07:00","id":1125186,"title":"","content":"Just had an epiphany here, but what level of narcissism does one need to have in order to think they're Daeva material? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hellovg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125137#post1125137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for Covenant, the Lancea et Sanctum all the way. Spirituality aside, the philosophy of it just makes sense to me...If I'm destined for corruption in unlife, best to hone it into a weapon with which to strike at the corruption I see in the world. Also, the access to various relics and histories, as well as the magic of Theban Sorcery would probably thrill my cold, dead, unbeating heart.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There is nothing about being a member of the Lancea et Sanctum that is required for dispensing vigilante justice. Other than the fact they would get pissy when it comes to 'freelance' workers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T13:51:13-07:00","id":1125336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125186#post1125186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just had an epiphany here, but what level of narcissism does one need to have in order to think they're Daeva material? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A touch less than the one that thinks they're Ventrue material, I imagine.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T14:02:55-07:00","id":1125345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Diggs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125336#post1125336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A touch less than the one that thinks they're Ventrue material, I imagine.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Meh, that one actually makes sense. If you've got the willpower, the ambition, and the skills to become a Ventrue, you should have no trouble proving your worth to them.<br /> <br /> With Daeva, you're pretty much saying <i>&quot;I'm so beautiful and creative, the world should be thankful for my presence!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T18:50:10-07:00","id":1125444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125345#post1125345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Meh, that one actually makes sense. If you've got the willpower, the ambition, and the skills to become a Ventrue, you should have no trouble proving your worth to them.<br /> <br /> With Daeva, you're pretty much saying <i>&quot;I'm so beautiful and creative, the world should be thankful for my presence!&quot;</i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>You know, I could say you're on to something if you said you would be a Gangrel or Mekhet. But since you've said you would be a Nossie, I can't help but think this just the age-old tale of Haunts being jealous of Serpents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-05T19:49:37-07:00","id":1125463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125444#post1125444\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You know, I could say you're on to something if you said you would be a Gangrel or Mekhet. But since you've said you would be a Nossie, I can't help but think this just the age-old tale of Haunts being jealous of Serpents. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind being a Gangrel, as pretty much all of their in clan disciplines appeal to me.<br /> <br /> My ancestor was an Arch Duke of France; which I guess technically makes me royalty?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But from a realistic perspective, Nosferatu are probably the only clan who'd see any potential value in me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm so pathetic!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-05-2017, 10:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T14:39:04-07:00","id":1125692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125463#post1125463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind being a Gangrel, as pretty much all of their in clan disciplines appeal to me.<br /> <br /> My ancestor was an Arch Duke of France; which I guess technically makes me royalty?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But from a realistic perspective, Nosferatu are probably the only clan who'd see any potential value in me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm so pathetic!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no no, I was just teasing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly, the Nosferatu are the clan who scare me the most. Not because they are the &quot;scary&quot; clan, but because they are in some ways the most unpredictable clan. They always find a use for everything and everybody, so if the other clans pass up on somebody who then gets turned into a Nosferatu, the other clans have done goofed because obviously there was something they all missed about this new Haunt that the Nosferatu noticed. And if any Clan puts Clan over politics every time, it's the Nosferatu. They take you no matter what, and they always have your back. They're like Requiem's creepy Hufflepuffs that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-06T16:35:21-07:00","id":1125728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1125692#post1125692\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no no, I was just teasing! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Honestly, the Nosferatu are the clan who scare me the most. Not because they are the &quot;scary&quot; clan, but because they are in some ways the most unpredictable clan. They always find a use for everything and everybody, so if the other clans pass up on somebody who then gets turned into a Nosferatu, the other clans have done goofed because obviously there was something they all missed about this new Haunt that the Nosferatu noticed. And if any Clan puts Clan over politics every time, it's the Nosferatu. They take you no matter what, and they always have your back. They're like Requiem's creepy Hufflepuffs that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, the Nossies are the kind of clan you can share a beer with... if they were able to drink beer.<br /> <br /> Though if I found out my warrens were patrolled by dog sized spiders, you can bet your ass that I would be sleeping in a private Haven!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https: