bcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1127270#post1127270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> We'll see how excitable they are when I combine a long tipped lighter with a can of Raid; frenzy check, be damned!</div> </div> </div> </div>What, and accidentally light yourself on fire while you panicked? That sounds like a silly thing to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T13:41:51-07:00","id":1127297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1127270#post1127270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> We'll see how excitable they are when I combine a long tipped lighter with a can of Raid; frenzy check, be damned!</div> </div> </div> </div>Better be Ordo, then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11492-arduras","name":"Arduras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11492_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T15:30:31-07:00","id":1127366,"title":"","content":"Something came to mind, though only recently. Since we all have a rather good idea of how we would be, or hope we would be, as Vampires I think it's time to ask the next logical thing: <br /> <br /> What do you think you would be like as an Elder? How do you think you would change s few hundred years from now? Admittedly that's an even more daunting question due to how difficult it is to even conceive of being around that long ( as a powerful blood sucking monstrosity no less), but a question worth asking!<br /> <br /> With me I see one of two things happening if I was able to be lucky enough to survive multiple centuries down the road; I would either embrace what it means to be Gangrel and truly try to do everything I could to be the apex of apex predators, possibly finally working to climb atop the mountain and become Prince of whatever city I dwelled in, ruling bloodily, but fairly as only a truly ascendant Gangrel could.<br /> <br /> Or.. perhaps I would search for a way to shed my Clan entirely ( likely through the Resilience Threnody) and attempt to build my own Clan- likely one heavily influenced by my love of Geist, creating a sort of Pseudo- Cappadocian/Giovanni type lineage that focuses on the underworld and Ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-10T19:38:37-07:00","id":1127449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1127366#post1127366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something came to mind, though only recently. Since we all have a rather good idea of how we would be, or hope we would be, as Vampires I think it's time to ask the next logical thing:<br /> <br /> What do you think you would be like as an Elder? How do you think you would change s few hundred years from now? Admittedly that's an even more daunting question due to how difficult it is to even conceive of being around that long ( as a powerful blood sucking monstrosity no less), but a question worth asking!<br /> <br /> With me I see one of two things happening if I was able to be lucky enough to survive multiple centuries down the road; I would either embrace what it means to be Gangrel and truly try to do everything I could to be the apex of apex predators, possibly finally working to climb atop the mountain and become Prince of whatever city I dwelled in, ruling bloodily, but fairly as only a truly ascendant Gangrel could.<br /> <br /> Or.. perhaps I would search for a way to shed my Clan entirely ( likely through the Resilience Threnody) and attempt to build my own Clan- likely one heavily influenced by my love of Geist, creating a sort of Pseudo- Cappadocian/Giovanni type lineage that focuses on the underworld and Ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tldr I become space Hollywood version of baron holger from night horrors<br /> Oh Wow, I probably finished acting as the archivist for the Savannah Bleak Annals as said before (Scholar), spent some time as a Carthain before becoming disillusioned with them, shepherded my descendants to a position I felt was comfortable for them (Shepard arc), actually used my history degree to explore my clan's history, meet some prehistoric Nosferatu who taught me some tricks and wrote some notes on the history and them (Archeologist), then wrote some novels based on those notes that became popular with the kine (artist) played a role in whatever led to the masquerade being gone in Infinite Macabre (puppet master), helped found KENT (Kindred Entertainment and News Television) , a vampire focused TV network/covenant sometime in the Cyberpunk era (Architect), and became famous by creating some of it's first hits and enjoyed the limelight as much as a nos can (Entertainer), then had an identity crisis regarding that limelight and headed off into space to find myself (Brute) before bringing that TV network interplanetary and entering the ISP market (Entrepreneur) and using that money to gain my position as the head of the Necropolis on some planet's equivalent to Hollywood and gotten back into writing for fun and profit. Along the way I would have sired four childer, the first one a mortal friend turned masquerade breach) ends up meeting the earthly sun due to my own irresponsibility, the 2nd ( who I embraced to gain a political ally in my movement days) turned on me when I left the movement and is now my enemy, the 3rd (one of my family's descendants who I lured into a nos scumdock using clues hidden in KENT broadcasts meant just for her) is a &quot;Casting Agent&quot; for KENT and the fourth (a winning audition) was taken by the owls to a distant moon. Any mortal who wants to join KENT as a Nos is welcome to enter the necropolis and &quot;audition&quot; to me, those who pass are embraced by me personally. Those who fail become blood in my belly.<br /> <br /> I would have gotten the Terrible Flesh devotion to the point of immobility and would be running the Nosferatu necropolis on that major media hub city of the galaxy using drones to experience the outside world, and a power mech walker for when I absolutely need to leave the necropolis. Personality wise, my mild paranoid streak has been enhanced by the long existence and thus My personal haven in the necropolis are filled with death traps and minions (both supernatural and robotic) for dealing with intruders, plus some ghouls to wash my thorax and bring me blood. I have my five ghoul dogs for companionship and protection and my huge computer in my haven where I write my stories for nights on end, monitor the necropolis spy on my ISP customers, micromanage my stable of TV stars and my mortal descendants and keep in touch with my fellow KENT moguls. My ability to draw connection between points of information that aren't obviously related has been honed to superhuman levels, to the point where it borders on precognition. On some level, I am still the idealist neonate that saw hope in the Carthains, and try to build a better (in my opinion) kindred society via my media influence, even as I benefit from the corrupt current order. My need to talk and hate of silence is fully indulged as I make my ghouls Liston to me rant on anything and everything.<br /> I am considering founding a bloodline, if I do their discipline reflects their nature as worms spinning webs of influence like conspiratorial spiders but their cause reflects my Physical dependence on others and mild paranoia<br /> Eventually my Terrible Flesh will reach the next stage and this worm will spin his cocoon, but what terrible bug will I hatch as?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 08-14-2017, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-11T01:04:32-07:00","id":1127518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1127366#post1127366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something came to mind, though only recently. Since we all have a rather good idea of how we would be, or hope we would be, as Vampires I think it's time to ask the next logical thing:<br /> <br /> What do you think you would be like as an Elder? How do you think you would change s few hundred years from now? Admittedly that's an even more daunting question due to how difficult it is to even conceive of being around that long ( as a powerful blood sucking monstrosity no less), but a question worth asking!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Without giving away too much information about my current mental health, I can say that I would become something utterly fucking horrifying as an elder. My clan, bloodline or covenant would have nothing to do with it. My mentality alone would be completely alien from anything recognizable as human.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Would I give into the Beast and descend into Draugr state? </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:14px\">Maybe, maybe not. But I definitely would not be somebody you'd want to get within 100 yards of.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-11-2017, 04:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T06:31:07-07:00","id":1128030,"title":"","content":"A rather difficult task, to determine what kind of Vampire I would be. But I shall try it, nonetheless.<br /> <br /> Clan : No idea<br /> <br /> I would like to say Gangrel, 'cause I've a temper (not really anger issues, but I'm not always the easiest person to be around) and I really love Gangrels... But I don't see myself attracting one's eye. I'm a strictly urban people who isn't really interested in physical activity. I'm rather average, physically and socially, so I think a Mekhet wanting an Infant able to blend relatively easily in his surrounding would chose me. Furthermore, I love to read about History, Religions, Cultures, Politics, Fantasy, Social Issues, like, a lot. And somehow I picture this passion as a typically Mekhet thing. Plus I've made studies in law, it's always convenient for a Kindred to have under his or her thumb. Hpefully, I would be a standard Mekhet, and not one of the stranger ones (or truly cursed ones, like the Morbus).<br /> <br /> No, scratch that. I'm not subtle enough to be a Mekhet. It's not that I solve my problem with force or something, but I like the direct approach more (and the big brutes in video games appeal to me more than subtle classes). Since I'm not important enough for a Ventrue, or beautiful enough for a Deava, I guess it let Nosferatu as an option, but, well, honestly, it can depend of the Vampire who would be Embracing me. He or she has his/her reasons, I don't get to chose my Clan after all !<br /> <br /> Covenant : I would probably be a part of Unaligned.<br /> <br /> I really like the Carthians (if they are more of the &quot;marxist&quot; variants, or at least &quot;leftists&quot;) and I like political discussions, but I'm not that invested into politics (I'm not a party member, I don't do militant activities beyond trying to convince friends/family on some issues), so I don't see myself able to join a Covenant who'se whole set up is politic. Perhaps, after some time, i would try to join the Ordo Dracul, since I'm interested into mysticism and all that, without the trappings of organized religion, but I think that it would rest mainly on how the local Dragons present themselves to potential aspirants. Learning that older vampires in this Covenant don't need to drink human blood under certain conditions would probably attract me to them very strongly. Of course, all of this rest upon the idea that my Sire wouldn't be part of a Covenant already, because I would probably be a part of this one (even some like the Invictus or the Lancea that I really don't agree with, or the Circle, which I could support if it isn't too much of a &quot;creed and doctrine&quot; approach). So, yep, Unaligned.<br /> <br /> Nightly routine : I would probably be one of those Vampire you don't hear much about. If you want some mortal informations on the surrounding, political evolutions and the like, I would trade it. I could probably make the messenger for young Vampires or ancillae (but not elders). I would try to carve myself a secure niche, and try not to make wave to protect it. I'm not a violent person, heck, I'm pretty sensitive (easily angry, but also easily moved to tears, laughs, you get it) so I would probably try to gather around peoples whom I may help despite feeding on them, such as those living in the slums in the making in my hometown : in exchange of their blood, I would try to make their lives better and help them ascend the social ladder generations after generations. I would also secretly seek any knowledge about the World of Darkness and its denizens, without trying to put myself into too much danger, of course.<br /> <br /> As an Elder : If I manage to survive to become an Elder, I would probably be this reclusive, know it all, ancient horror with a lot of human families, either powerful or not, at my beck and call. Of course, my already existing streak of paranoia would have grown exponentially, so I would probably be very hard to contact or to convince to spill some information.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","user":"Ur-Than","date":". 08-12-2017, 10:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1233-ur-than","name":"Ur-Than","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T08:07:51-07:00","id":1128049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_con