npredictable. You could bind me with a Ban and a Bane, but if you pushed me hard enough I doubt the backlash of breaking a Ward would hold me back. My Frenzy burns cold, so you don't know it's happened until you're already dead. Somewhere along the path from Neonate to Ancilla to Elder I would grow to be more accepting of violence, and actively hone my own skills. The Khaibit actually fit me quite nicely. Diligence and loyalty paired with brutal efficiency. The might of Disciplines adding onto centuries of time to hone my martial arts skills from hobby and art form into something that makes me more than capable of protecting myself despite the &amp;quot;Friendly Neighbourhood Vampire&amp;quot; exterior. I would fade into darkness, into obscurity, from all except those who would seek me out. But that doesn't mean that I'm not watching. Maybe I'll amuse myself by walking unnoticed and unseen with Obfuscate. The rush of surprise from my seemingly harmless Mask concealing a brutal machine of a monster will have faded now that people know what I look like. Ah well, simple pleasures. It's the little things that stave off ennui after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, did not peg you as the overly peaceful type. Well the more you know! You sound super interesting as a vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T08:27:00-07:00","id":1129799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129764#post1129764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, did not peg you as the overly peaceful type. Well the more you know! You sound super interesting as a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not so much &quot;overly peaceful&quot; as &quot;strongly adverse to causing lasting physical harm&quot;. I have absolutely no problem practicing martial arts or sparring, but I don't take advantage of opportunities I can see to take control of a fight because I don't like the risk it presents to the other person.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad you think I'm interesting, but I don't personally think so. What's so interesting about me as a vampire?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:06:30-07:00","id":1129816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129799#post1129799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not so much &amp;quot;overly peaceful&amp;quot; as &amp;quot;strongly adverse to causing lasting physical harm&amp;quot;. I have absolutely no problem practicing martial arts or sparring, but I don't take advantage of opportunities I can see to take control of a fight because I don't like the risk it presents to the other person.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad you think I'm interesting, but I don't personally think so. What's so interesting about me as a vampire?</div> </div> </div> </div>As a practitioner myself, I understand that bit a great deal. Still, that is overly peaceful to me, as self-defense isn't the only reason to practice :3<br /> <br /> And it's interesting due to you being a scary &quot;vampire next door&quot;, I love those type of vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:22:33-07:00","id":1129826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129659#post1129659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... me as a vampire?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't be so sure that you'd lose control. Remember, the Mekhet embody grace and finesse. They probably have better self control than any of the other clans (monsters, savages, hedonists, aristocrats). For a clan who likes to take the subtle approach, a non lethal take down would be more preferable to, say, ripping a man's head off.<br /> <br /> And dislocating somebody's arm isn't that big a deal. Sure, it's painful as hell, but it's actually pretty easy to fix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:40:59-07:00","id":1129838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129826#post1129826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't be so sure that you'd lose control. Remember, the Mekhet embody grace and finesse. They probably have better self control than any of the other clans (monsters, savages, hedonists, aristocrats). For a clan who likes to take the subtle approach, a non lethal take down would be more preferable to, say, ripping a man's head off.<br /> <br /> And dislocating somebody's arm isn't that big a deal. Sure, it's painful as hell, but it's actually pretty easy to fix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, fair enough assessment. Yay, undeath would be potentially not horrendously awful?<br /> <br /> I would still be a bloodsucking monstrosity, but at least I'd be a composed and self-controlled monstrosity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T09:57:58-07:00","id":1129851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129838#post1129838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, fair enough assessment. Yay, undeath would be potentially not horrendously awful?<br /> <br /> I would still be a bloodsucking monstrosity, but at least I'd be a composed and self-controlled monstrosity.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just think of yourself as a ninja. Even on the job, they only killed as a last resort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T10:10:02-07:00","id":1129855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129838#post1129838\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, fair enough assessment. Yay, undeath would be potentially not horrendously awful?<br /> <br /> I would still be a bloodsucking monstrosity, but at least I'd be a composed and self-controlled monstrosity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would like to point out that even if you focus all of your willpower and self discipline to avoid Frenzy, the Beast breaking free is Inevitable. Maybe it only happens one a year, a decade, a century... but it will get out. Still, if it's only rarely, it's far better than some other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 08-16-2017, 01:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T11:27:24-07:00","id":1129900,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"4152\" data-vbnamecard=\"4152\">Arcanist</a> as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> pointed out, Ninja is a pretty good comparison. Not the movie type, the original ones who were basically spies with some additional skills most people didn't know about. Except you'd be a more-or-less-friendly-Neigbhourhood Vampire =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:04:46-07:00","id":1129916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129855#post1129855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point out that even if you focus all of your willpower and self discipline to avoid Frenzy, the Beast breaking free is Inevitable. Maybe it only happens one a year, a decade, a century... but it will get out. Still, if it's only rarely, it's far better than some other vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no, perfectly aware that I'd lose it eventually. Might even <i>want </i>to, depending on the circumstances, but rarely is still better than frequently.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar8542_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"8542\" data-vbnamecard=\"8542\">Wormwood</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> Ninja is a pretty good way of looking at it. And hey, isn't that how a lot of people play the Khaibit anyways?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T12:16:32-07:00","id":1129922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129916#post1129916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, perfectly aware that I'd lose it eventually. Might even <i>want </i>to, depending on the circumstances, but rarely is still better than frequently.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Ninja is a pretty good way of looking at it. And hey, isn't that how a lot of people play the Khaibit anyways?</div> </div> </div> </div>I sort of play them as dark bounty hunters personally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-16T19:49:12-07:00","id":1130096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arcanist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1129916#post1129916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no, perfectly aware that I'd lose it eventually. Might even <i>want </i>to, depending on the circumstances, but rarely is still better than frequently.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everybody wants to lose it sometimes. We're not exactly saints, here.<br /> <br /> The important thing is your ability to recognize why it's a bad thing to do so. Means you're not completely disconnected from humanity. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:42:45-07:00","id":1131989,"title":"","content":"*boop*<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://encrypted-tbn0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcRG41Vx6szDWUCQJY2JlL6kWEvkfag-ncsR6Jg7B0ZU3AAGp3v58A\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Where is everybody? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T18:59:27-07:00","id":1131993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1131989#post1131989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is everybody? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've mostly been waiting for the conversation to start up again. Been looking over the vampire stuff to build some homebrew covenants and elders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:29:17-07:00","id":1132001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1131993#post1131993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've mostly been waiting for the conversation to start up again. Been looking over the vampire stuff to build some homebrew covenants and elders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, over on Werewolf, Koroga mentioned possibly starting the Mage version; but that was like 2 or 3 days ago.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T19:29:41-07:00","id":1132002,"title":"","content":"I have an idea maybe to relaunch the conversation. <br /> Say if you ... as a vampire could start a bloodline what would it look like? What would be the parent clan, extra discipline, bloodline gift and bloodline curse?<br /> I'll give myself the night to think on it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-20T21:20:31-07:00","id":1132052,"title":"","content":"Well, I guess if this thread is in need of a resurrection, I can help out!<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Daeva, or possibly Mekhet<br /> <br /> <i>Reason: </i>I feel like I absolutely fit the bill for one of the Daeva. Although I consider myself more friendly than anything, I've had more than a handful of people tell me I come across as very flirtatious, which is completely unintentional. The Wanton Curse speaks to me, though, as I am no stranger to hard-and-fast, consuming relationships, and how innocent they can start, and how unstable they can become. I'm a natural orator, I feel like, and my group of friends will frequently have me recite old nightly-adventures for that extra &quot;oomph&quot; to the story's memory. With my ability to draw attention, I feel like I'd be a natural with Majesty, too. Also, not that it matters for the Serpents, I am more-than-conventionally attractive, which has its share of boons &amp; banes (manipulation/persuasion is easier, but man is that objectification is a bitch). Lastly, I've been told I'm passionate in my day-to-day interactions, though I contribute that more to my severe ADHD than anything. I like to think of myself as enough of a social chameleon as being able to get along with most types of people (so long as they're...yah know...decent in the modern sense). <br /> <br /> Part of me feels like I'd also be a pretty good fit with the Mekhet, barring their reputation as the most cosmopolitan of clans. I feel very dual-sided, in life, and while I certainly have more than my fair share of being a social butterfly, I also have a far more introverted side that I've especially embraced in the last few years. The strangeness in the Mekhet blood reverberates with me too, and I frequently flirt with the idea of simply disappearing, so I feel like I'd abuse Obfuscate to that end. Auspex strikes me as a potential double-edged sword, but its a valuable tool. I've always been to drawn to shadows, and the occult, and I doubt the darkness having real horrors within that could harm me would stop me from digging deeper. I feel like a Mekhet elder would really appreciate that aspect about me.<br /> <br /> Then again, I'm *really* loud, both vocally, and personality-wise, and I doubt that'd appeal to most Shadows, haha.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant: </b>Carthians, or Circle of the Crone <br /> <br /> <i>Reason: </i>Oh boy. I'm a firebrand by nature, and while I consider myself a progressive anarchist more than anything at this point, I feel like my rabble rousing would catch more than an eye or two within the Movement, probably for exploitation, but whatever. I also enjoy writing, and I dabble in art, so I feel like in my night-to-night I'd be deep in spreading the Cacophony around the city, which is tied closely with the Carthians &amp; the Daeva, it seems. While I enjoy the idea of the Invictus aesthetically, I couldn't bear with the stuffy, conservative collars most of their domains would try to wrap around my neck. Though, I guess by consigning myself to the Carthians, I'd be making an underdog out of myself, either way. <br /> <br /> On the other side of the coin, I feel like I'd really enjoy the Circle of the Crone. As I mentioned, I've always been drawn to the occult, and I have more than a few friends who are themselves witches, so I doubt it'd be much of a learning curve to worship some esoteric God. Besides, the idea of embracing one's vampire nature is very appealing, and while I know the Ordo Dracul also has &quot;occult-y&quot; vibes, their whole &quot;transcend the vampire condition&quot; doesn't appeal to me, and the Coils seem like a lot of work for little pay-off. Also, Cruac is far too tempting, in that eldritch-in-a-carnal kind of way, for me to just ignore. Especially after reading SotC.<br /> <br /> Then again, I might just say screw it and stay Unbound. I would be a Neonate after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14044-kingbuji","name":"kingbuji","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14044_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T02:31:26-07:00","id":1132133,"title":"","content":"A loud Mekhet, huh? That's an interesting concept, actually. Hiding in plain sight, taking refuge in audacity... being a social Chameleon would REALLY help with all that spying!<br /> <br /> Regarding Bloodline, I think I'd most likely make a Covenant-exclusive one, and since I most likely would end up in the Ordo Dracul, that would be just the thing. Parent clan Gangrel, I assume. I could see collecting Collecting Information as an additional Discipline, so let's go with Auspex. Bloodline gift would be a bonus to Perception and Inspection rolls, to go with the &quot;notices stuff&quot; angle. The Clan curse would be probably be being easily distracted, losing track of goals because of new information.<br /> Alternatively, Obfuscate would be the the additional Discipline.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that would be my first take on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T03:47:55-07:00","id":1132151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1132133#post1132133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding Bloodline, I think I'd most likely make a Covenant-exclusive one,</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, if I'm going to make my own bloodline and not join the ranks of the vampire bogeymen, it would most likely be aligned with the Circle.<br /> <br /> I don't even try to deny the fact I'm a hedonist, which means there's a good chance my bloodline would be a pack of Nosferatu with access to Majesty. The bloodline's flaw in this particular case would be inheriting my fickle attention span, causing them to feverishly chase after their object of desire before rapidly growing bored with it and seeking a new form of entertainment.<br /> <br /> Our private rituals among the Circle of the Crone would be filled with decadence and pleasure. And since we are a family of Nosferatu, I'm going to assume that the debauchery reaches into territory even the Daeva are hesitant to touch. We would be a bloodline with power over both <b>fear</b> and <b>desire</b>, manipulating mortal and kindred alike with a maddened gleam in our eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> I told you, you wouldn't want to be within 100 yards of me as an Elder... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 08-21-2017, 07:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T09:47:09-07:00","id":1132247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1132001#post1132001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, over on Werewolf, Koroga mentioned possibly starting the Mage version; but that was like 2 or 3 days ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my fault, I got super busy with work/ looking over Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:01:24-07:00","id":1132253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1132247#post1132247\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was my fault, I got super busy with work/ looking over Mage.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I understand.<br /> <br /> Anyways, I went ahead and started the Beast thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1132144-you-as-a-beast\">You as a Beast</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:01:40-07:00","id":1132255,"title":"","content":"I'd be the quintessential Mekhet: I take secrets, I give nothing in return. The &quot;twist&quot; is that people usually tell me their personal stories without me asking. Never understood that.<br /> <br /> As for Covenant, I'd probably lean towards the Ordo, because I'm not very fit for politics, or the necessary niceties of politics, and I'm already in academia so at least I understand that habitat. Also, I'm studying to be a doctor, so maybe I could actually be &quot;useful&quot; to the covenant? Mind you, I'm trying to be a radiologist, so I won't amount to much other than asking &quot;What happens when a vampire uses disciplines during an MRI scan?&quot;. Failing the Ordo, I'd opt to be a pretty useless Carthian, just there to make numbers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Italian nuisance. English is my second language, so be patient!<br /> <br /> <b>My homebrew:</b><br /> <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/270766-domain-light-from-a-dead-star-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">[VtR 2e] Light From a Dead Star: Rome</span></a></b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1117941-hunting-ground-the-past-is-another-country-rome\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#8B4513\"><b>[WtF 2e] The Past Is Another Country: Rome</b></span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3765-snesferatu","name":"SNESferatu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3765_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-21T10:50:27-07:00","id":1132291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SNESferatu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1132255#post1132255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd be the quintessential Mekhet: I take secrets, I give nothing in return. The &quot;twist&quot; is that people usually tell me their personal stories without me asking. Never understood that.<br /> <br /> As for Covenant, I'd probably lean towards the Ordo, because I'm not very fit for politics, or the necessary niceties of politics, and I'm already in academia so at least I understand that habitat. Also, I'm studying to be a doctor, so maybe I could actually be &quot;useful&quot; to the covenant? Mind you, I'm trying to be a radiologist, so I won't amount to much other than asking &quot;What happens when a vampire uses disciplines during an MRI scan?&quot;. Failing the Ordo, I'd opt to be a pretty useless Carthian, just there to make numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;What happens to the Kindred body when exposed to different kinds of radiation?&quot; &quot;What do you see on an MRI scan on a passive Kindred? What about Torpored? When using [Discipline A/B/C]?&quot;<br /> &quot;I want to see a bone regrowing. For Reasons. Lend me your lab (access) and/or skills?&quot; &quot;Hey, I want to fry human blood and Vitae of different potency with x-rays to compare what happens. You in?&quot;<br /> &quot;Running an experiment on bloodlines/the embrace. Need Subjects with [Problem X], e.g. brain tumor patients would be fine. You got some files for me?&quot;<br /> &quot;Wanna follow the flow of Blood for a social experiment. Can I borrow some radioactive markers?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, dude. What do we look like in ultrasound?&quot; &quot;I heard radiated Vitae is more potent when using it for [Discipline x] or [Blood Bonding]. Contaminate me? Please?&quot;<br /> &quot;Let's check out what changes to your Vitae when you have mastered the Coils of the Voivode. I run some tests with bacteria, you do the radiation thing, Sebastian does the chemical analysis, alright?&quot;<br /> &quot;Hey, is there a way to mark the Princes's Herd's blood? I think someone is sneaking some of it, and I want to know who.&quot;<br /> &quot;I want to embrace a childer. Prince said it's okay. But I want to make it useful - get all the data we can get during the whole procedure. Wanna see the embrace on MRI or CT?&quot;<br /> <br /> And you say you wouldn't be useful. Don't underestimate your fellow Dragons' creativity! =D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-24T05:33:54-07:00","id":1133335,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;What has science doooooone!?&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-28T22:10:07-07:00","id":1135066,"title":"","content":"<b>Clan</b>: Gangrel without a doubt. I'm so tied down to my apartment that I would love to fly free, sleep in the earth and not be tied down to a haven. <br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Ordo Dracul most of the time. Spending half my nights trying to transcend the Curse, while spending the rest exploring weird haunts would keep me engaged enough to avoid facing the sun.<br /> <br /> While I am a socialist in life, I'd most likely align with whichever political covenant is in power. I have no interest in being killed for the Revolution or swatted by an Invictus Elder chessmaster. <br /> <br /> I'm not at all into the idea of being God's damned monster, so I'd stay away from the Spear and the Chapel.<br /> <br /> I'd be utterly terrified of the Circle of the Crone, but my curiosity regarding their occult knowledge would entice me to maybe do a little gardening and sorcery with them on occasion. <br /> <br /> <b>Nightly Business</b>: Sneaking into weird places looking for Dragon's Nests. Developing Protean and the Mystery of the Ascendant. Delicately avoiding the topic of experimenting on people to develop Scales of the Dragon. The niche I'd fill in the All Night Society? Support staff. I'd make sure it was my business to know everything about the city and be on good terms with people who control vital resources. I've always been good at that sort of thing at work. I keep my grudges bottled up, and I don't start pointless fights with people, and I remember how and where to access resources. &quot;Oh you've had that haircut and nasty scar for 50 years? I know just the Night Doctor for you.&quot; &quot;Look, I know the Prince thinks he's carved you out of all the feeding territories, but there's this little suburb I know that had all their Kindred wiped out in a freak Werewolf attack. No no no, you don't need to worry, I have it on good authority that it was a personal conflict. Just...don't be obvious.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Elder</b>: I'd be tempted to skip whole swaths of history, especially if my blood gets too thick to easily operate. I'd have my mortal family and their descendents as a touchstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T14:27:46-08:00","id":1160651,"title":"","content":"This is going to be the hardest one for me, as I find vampire to be the least interesting. However, I will do my best.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: I'm not exactly comfortable selecting a clan, since nothing about my personality or agency has anything to do with which clan I become. I just have to wait and see who embraces me and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> If I could choose, I would go with <b>Mekhet</b>. The boons that come with the Mekhet clan suit my personality and nature quite nicely, while the tenebrous curse would have the weakest impact on my personality and sense of agency. Being so tightly controlled by my Beast (as a Gangrel) or by my base urges (as a Daeva) is intimidating to me, and I would rather not have to deal with those curses.<br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: In Werewolf, I said I would go with Storm Lords or Iron Masters, while in Mage I said I would go Silver Ladder or Free Council. Generally speaking I am the sort of person who takes responsibility and leadership seriously, and I will take leadership positions if I felt it necessary to do so.<br /> <br /> However, when it comes to vampire politics, I simply don't care enough. As such, I would most likely join the <b>Ordo Dracul</b>. It has a nice sort of academic feel to it, and it is nice and disconnected from the rest of vampire politics. If I truly felt it necessary to involve myself in that sort of politics, I would go with Invictus... but probably not.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightly Business</b>: What I would want to do is become a scholar. Chances are it would take some time before I could really harness the power and resources to do it effectively - I probably couldn't just walk up to an elder vampire and be like &quot;oh, by the way, I want to be a scholar and do research, so don't send me off to serve as your carrier pigeon. I'd be more effective if you let me manage your library.&quot; I'll do what is necessary keep alive and do my best to gather knowledge and favours as I go. If that means be a courier, then I'll be your courier. Need a scout? I'm your scout. Need a spy? I can do that, I'm quiet enough for the job. Just as long as I can find the time to indulge my curiosities about the vampire condition - oh, and maybe just don't throw me into the middle of a big war or battle or anything like that? I like being alive, or undead as it were.<br /> <br /> I would most immediately be interested in studying the properties of Vitae and would work towards becoming a sort of Hematologist - or Blood Scientist. Becoming a supernatural creature of any sort really just opens up my understanding of the natural world. As a vampire, undeath and the power of vitae are now covered in the natural world, and I would be interested in studying it. The supernatural slants to it are not satisfying to me, and the way that vitae loses its properties over time until it becomes just a mix of ordinary blood would frustrate my efforts, but perhaps something about the vampire condition would allow me to study it in a meaningful way. I would be interested in inventing tools that let me investigate the supernatural elements of the world and better understand its interaction with the natural world. I could also see myself really studying disciplines, since they are fuelled by Vitae and as such are intimately connected to Vitae - it is the power of the blood that allows for the use of these disciplines. I would like to study them all and potentially discover new disciplines - find new ways to exploit the power of Vitae.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'd end up making my own covenant/covenant-like organization - one that is more focused on studying the vampiric condition using the scientific method. I would also be interested in studying other supernatural creatures in this way as well - assuming I were powerful enough to subdue a suitable test subject. At the very least, I would ultimately like to have a secret lab where my neonates and I conduct our research. I would set up blood clinics as a front for collecting blood for research purposes. I would be interested in discovering a way to preserve vitae (such that it doesn't expire within minutes). Of course, as I answer questions, more are likely to come up, but that is to be expected.<br /> <br /> Allow me to keep to my little corner of the world, and you will find that I am no bother. Any help you are willing to offer (resources, manpower, test subjects, blood) is much appreciated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T16:13:20-08:00","id":1160679,"title":"","content":"My favorite clan is the one I'd end up being. I am a martial artist in real life. I've been studying Kashima Shin-ryu Kenjutsu for the past 18 years. As a martial artist I've always been a patient and methodical person and as a vampire I would strive to be a cautious individual. I like observing from a distance before joining any groups or making any friends and I have an obsessive need to know everything about my circle, what they're doing, and who they are. If I can't trust someone I usually ditch them like a bad habit and loyalty is the most important trait that a person can possess. In most &quot;Choose your power games.&quot; I usually always pick something akin to &quot;Knowing if someone is lying to me.&quot; or &quot;Knowing people's secrets.&quot; and Auspex fits this greatly. Not to mention the privacy that obfuscate affords is not to be underestimated.<br /> <br /> That being said..<br /> <br /> Covenant would have to be Ordo Dracul. I desire to know and am constantly obsessed with learning. At no time in my life have I ever felt &quot;I know enough.&quot; because there's no such thing as &quot;Knowing enough.&quot; There is always more room for improvement, more room for mastery, and if I was a vampire I would dedicate everything to removing the weaknesses that would make my life difficult. The first time someone comes to me and offers a true proven plan to remove the negative aspects of my condition they would gain my support wholeheartedly. A covenant devoted to self improvement, mastery, and ascension is right up my alley./<br /> <br /> Nightly Activities: I would strive to be the best vampire I could be and do whatever it takes to make the most of my unlife. I would want to ensure I am skilled enough to protect myself from outside threats. Especially given I would then know that there are other supernatural beings out there but I wouldn't focus exclusively on combat. I would also take my time to master hunting, feeding, securing a haven, and have enough city status in order to ensure a comfortable requiem. I would make it my mission to find what I can on all the neighboring vampires but I wouldn't use it for black mail as that is an easy way to make enemies. Instead, I'd use it as a shield if any of them come after me by making it a point if they were to hurt me everyone would find out (insert skeleton in the closet here.). On the side I'd be developing as many coils as I could and offer to teach what I know about swordsmanship to any interested Kindred. As I get comfortable I would begin creating ghouls in order to run my mortal affairs as well as to provide a steady bit of income.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":22996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22996-mekhet-unlife","user":"Mekhet Unlife","date":". 11-19-2017, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22996-mekhet-unlife","name":"Mekhet Unlife","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22996_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T22:53:05-08:00","id":1160775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>oeruli</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1160651#post1160651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to be the hardest one for me, as I find vampire to be the least interesting. However, I will do my best.<br /> <br /> <b>Clan</b>: I'm not exactly comfortable selecting a clan, since nothing about my personality or agency has anything to do with which clan I become. I just have to wait and see who embraces me and hope for the best.<br /> <br /> If I could choose, I would go with <b>Mekhet</b>. The boons that come with the Mekhet clan suit my personality and nature quite nicely, while the tenebrous curse would have the weakest impact on my personality and sense of agency. Being so tightly controlled by my Beast (as a Gangrel) or by my base urges (as a Daeva) is intimidating to me, and I would rather not have to deal with those curses.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We're not so much &quot;choosing&quot; our clan, but rather, we're proposing which clan we believe would be best interested in embracing us.<br /> <br /> A big part of answering these requires introspection and evaluating ourselves. After careful consideration, I realized the Nosferatu are the only clan in Requiem that would have even a passing interest in embracing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 11-20-2017, 01:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T04:27:57-08:00","id":1160806,"title":"","content":"A misfit Gangrle that is probably driven insane in isolation or killed by my Sire for being a disappointment. I have no question that I would die pretty fast if I was Embraced.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T04:45:07-08:00","id":1160809,"title":"","content":"Clan: Since I like reading up on stuff, researching, and sometimes simply clicking through the net to get know stuff, I like to correlate information, thus Mekhet would probably fit best. I don't think I could offer anything to another clan. Even though, personally, I like the Daeva best.<br /> <br /> Covenant: At early years I would have chosen the Circle of the Crone, but opinions change. Lancea Sanctum is too religious, and the Ordo Dracul too monstrous, the Carthians too rebellious for my taste. I would probably join the Invictus for the stability they offer, and protecting the Masquerade is a worthwhile cause. After gaining age and experience, I would probably go Unbound, fed up with covenant business.<br /> <br /> Nightlife: Probably watching and correlating news regarding Masquerade breaches, and also analyzing current events on how to find out, if a vampire is involved. For fun: going out and remaining unseen.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1681-murder-of-crows","name":"Murder-of-Crows","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1681_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T09:21:45-08:00","id":1160884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1121995-you-as-a-vampire?p=1160775#post1160775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We're not so much &quot;choosing&quot; our clan, but rather, we're proposing which clan we believe would be best interested in embracing us.<br /> <br /> A big part of answering these requires introspection and evaluating ourselves. After careful consideration, I realized the Nosferatu are the only clan in Requiem that would have even a passing interest in embracing me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that these are exercises in introspection. The problem is that introspection isn't useful at determining the agenda of anyone other than myself - especially an immortal vampire. Part of my introspective process here was understanding that I ultimately do not get to choose.<br /> <br /> It says in the description of the Mekhet the following things that leave me hollow about making the choice:<br /> - Anyone can be Embraced by a Mekhet, but those newly dead minds find themselves hungry for mental stimulation and consumed by curiosity.<br /> - Even a cement-footed klutz in life finds that, after the Mekhet Embrace, people say things to him like, &quot;Oh! I didn't see you there&quot;<br /> <br /> Even people who do not fit the Mekhet in life will do so in death. With Werewolf I can base my auspice on my personality for the most part and have a good chance of being correct. With Mage I can base my path on my personality and lifestyle - while anything can happen, one Path seems more likely the way things are going at the moment. With vampire, I have the whims of other vampires.<br /> <br /> Which of course leaves me with one conclusion: I can introspect as much as I want, but it's not about me. It's about the sire. Even though I am already naturally curious and quiet to the point that being Mekhet would feel more of an enhancement than a curse, any vampire at any moment could be interested in me for any reason.<br /> <br /> I am open to the possibility that I just don't know enough about Vampire. As I said, I find it to be the least interesting (this was included in the quote from me). If I were to gain a better understanding of what makes a vampire interested in a potential childe, I could incorporate that in my introspective process and provide a better answer.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, I have thought about it a little more and have the following addendum. If I am to go with &quot;<i>vampires are interested in people who exhibit traits of their clan, and so I should match my personality and experience with the clan that is the closest fit</i>&quot;, then I stand by <b>Mekhet</b>. Possibly <b>Ventrue</b> due to my background and my stance towards leadership. If I am to go with &quot;<i>vampires like their childe to feel like they are suffering a curse</i>&quot; then <b>Daeva</b> or <b>Gangrel</b>. If its &quot;<i>vampires embrace people who they think will be useful in whatever scheme they are planning</i>&quot; then it could be anything, especially if said vampire sends an agent to do it instead of doing it himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21757-oeruli","name":"oeruli","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T18:05:42-08:00","id":1161360,"title":"","content":"I see where you are coming from Oeruli. If it really comes down to the whims of others though, can I suggest you roll a dice (1 is you die in the embrace. Or reroll. :P ) and you become whatever clan corresponds with whatever number.<br /> <br /> THEN YOU INTROSPECT! :3<br /> <br /> On topic, and I'll expand later in a different post:<br /> <br /> <b>Clan:</b> Agree with Oeruli. Still, fancy myself a Venture. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <i><b>HOWEVER, SEE BELOW!</b></i><br /> <br /> <b>Covenant</b>: Vampire University or Vampire Incorporated. (Ordo or Invictus)<br /> <br /> <b>Bloodline:</b> Non-committal. Wouldn't do it until someone revealed I could forge one. Then I'd make a bloodline.<br /> <br /> <b>Disciplines:</b> All of them, favoring those that let me experience new ways of being. Possession, protean, projection, and all the devotions I could dream up.<br /> <br /> <b>Dirge: </b>Undead Philosopher of the French variety. (Which basically means I'd spend my life fucking around with different ideologies while trying to live(?) passionately.)<br /> <br /> <b>Mask:</b> Investor/Executive. (Dominate would be useful here to set up the sham version but I guess a vampire has no inherent advantage over a mortal if they want to do the real thing and this would keep it interesting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> -----<br /> <br /> Edit time.<br /> <br /> So I did as I recommended Oeruli should do, and rolled off. My result: Gangrel bait. So how might that change the above?<br /> <br /> Well, it doesn't massively. I'm still me. However, it would have some impact that I didn't expect.<br /> <br /> I am a rather abstract kind of person; instinct doesn't look good on me. My sexuality is weird and creepy, my dancing is awful, and my angry voice, even when angry, doesn't have an weight to it. So the sociopathic perspective of the Mekhet and Venture suit me, in that it would be familiar skin.<br /> <br /> Not Gangrel. Oh boy.<br /> <br /> In a way, the Beast I gain in dead might make me feel the most alive I have ever felt. And that would be disturbing. Very disturbing. Whereas with all the other clans, I might fall into 'dark superhero' beliefs early on ('I can force others to obey me. Neat.'), I think the Gangrel Beast would trip that up. I'd have to wrestle with myself, and the fancy power I have doesn't affect others; it warps me. As such, I expect I'd become very introspective. I mentioned a Dirge of French Philosophy; well Gangrel Tabanese would be gathering all those blasted books on Being and going to town. I expected I'd spend a lot of time self-examining; thinking about what it meant to have a Beast.<br /> <br /> I'd be inclined to believe that it was a new set of instincts; that I couldn't commit to a substance dualism. That would make the Circle more palatable but again, spiritualism isn't my cup of tea. I'd toy with what the curse was though and I'd start earnestly investigating the paranormal again. Really though, it is my world view that would be the main object of investigation; I wouldn't want examples of paranormal but justifications for their place in the world. I know it makes me sound like a zealot but my reaction to 'undeath' wouldn't change my belief in the afterlife or God at all. I KNOW, with argument that is unconcerned with particulars, that those things don't make sense. And with so much changing, I'd likely grip those beliefs more, not less. So a philosophical Gangrel obsessed with the nature of Being, the Beast, and Man.<br /> <br /> Honestly, without the toys that the other clans get, and with the sudden drives that push me, Gangrel Tabanese might end up being the most academic of the clans. And that, to me, is a fun thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2003,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","user":"Tabanese","date":". 11-22-2017, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2003-tabanese","name":"Tabanese","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2003_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"282"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}